<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Keleshbey Chachba</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1808">1808</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Kelesh Ahmed-Bey Shervashidze</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Keleshbey <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-shervashidze">Chachba</a>, also called Kelesh Ahmed-Bey Shervashidze, was prince of Abkhazia in the late 18th and early 19th centuries. A Muslim ruler under Ottoman overlordship, he built up princely power, controlled the port of Sukhum and dealt with both the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>. He was assassinated in 1808, and his son Giorgi then placed the principality under Russian protection in 1810.</p></div>
